// Scope a single rule to several tools by listing them in a Cedar
// set on the action position with `in`. The new idea: one rule can
// cover multiple Drupe actions without duplication.
//
// The body is empty here because each listed action has its own
// input shape, and a body that referenced `context.input.shares`
// would not type-check against `GetStockInfo`-style actions. See
// 0104 for the single-action form that unlocks tool-specific
// input fields.

permit (
    principal,
    action in [Drupe::Action::"SellShares", Drupe::Action::"ApproveSale"],
    resource
);
